WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.470
Oh, hello.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.850
I didn't see you there
because I'm in a video.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.110
I'm just out driving my
foreign-owned boat ship,

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.640
but not between American ports

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.070
because of a little thing
called the Jones Act.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.710
100-year old protectionists law

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.840
that makes traffic worse
and stuff more expensive.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.920
Not to be confused with the
Davy Jones Act, which requires

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.290
that all haunted pirates live
on the floor of the ocean

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.470
or the Alex Jones Act,
which requires everyone

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.030
to wear protective head foil
when discussing frog genders.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.030
No, the Jones Act requires
that any vessels sailing

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.010
between American ports
must be American built,

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.350
American owned, manned
by an American crew,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.700
flying the American flag.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.200
If your ship has a maple leaf on it

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.170
or a falcon strangling an eel,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.450
or whatever this guy is up to,

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.350
you cannot go between American
ports to sell us cheap stuff

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.630
from your country, or even transport stuff

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.300
from our country to other
parts of our country.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.390
The Jones Act regulates cabotage,
which prior to this video,

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.940
I assumed was some kind
of floating cabbage,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.920
but it turns out, no, cabotage is the act

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.950
of shipping goods between two
ports within the same country.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.050
So if you wanna sail
from Denver to Las Vegas

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.560
on a foreign ship, you'd
be a moron (buzzer buzzing)

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.670
because the Jones Act restricts cabotage

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.020
to American vessels.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.120
By limiting which ships can schlep stuff

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.050
in between our ports, it
makes shipping more expensive,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.070
which makes stuff more expensive.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:25.410
Particularly for places like
Hawaii, Puerto Rico, Guam

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.020
or any new floaty states
I haven't got around

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.140
to learning about yet.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.750
The Jones Act exists under the pretense

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.860
of national defense because of Germans.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.990
During World War I, European
commercial ships normally used

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.150
to transport top hats and laudanum

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.830
to feed hungry Americans,
not got yanked out

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.790
from our shipping lanes
to assist the war effort.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:45.360
Those ships were stuck in Europe,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.960
varying bayonets and nunchucks
back and forth trying

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.670
to kill evil Archduke Franz Ferdinand.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.680
Don't worry, we got him.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.080
After the War, the
United States got worried

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.470
that a global interconnected economy,

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.820
like the one we currently enjoy

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.390
which has lifted billions out of poverty,

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.940
would mean having to rely on foreign ships

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.620
which might suddenly skip
out on commercial shipping

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.560
during the inevitable return
of zombie Franz Ferdinand.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.010
Worse yet, American politicians threaded

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.090
that the next time we went to
a war on a distant continent,

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.260
we might not have enough
ships to transport cannons

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.010
or horses or horse cannons.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.010
We needed to figure out a way

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.870
to ensure we had enough American ships

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.630
to get in on that horse war.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:28.730
So we passed the Jones Act in
1920, forbidding foreign ships

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.330
from operating between our ports.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.620
It's the economic equivalent of saying,

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.910
Jiffy Lube closed once

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:36.440
so we all better learn
how to change our own oil.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.770
So let's ban Jiffy Lube
in case it closes again.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.030
The Jones Act and the little
tweaks we've added to it

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.370
over the years is rife with protectionism.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.760
For example, when American-owned
ships are repaired,

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.250
only 10% of the steel can be foreign,

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.900
90% of that steel better
be from the United States.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.120
Foreign steel is too
flimsy and too foreign,

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.530
it's basically shiny cheese.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:01.160
Protectionism has a big problem
though, it doesn't work.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.690
By outlawing foreign ships from cabotage,

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.380
the Jones Act limits the
amount of available ships

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.670
which drives up the cost of shipping.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.690
Driving up the cost of shipping,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.000
make shipping more expensive.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.600
That would be the supply
of law and demand.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.990
With less demand for shipping,

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:19.640
shipping companies purchase fewer vessels

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.330
which means fewer boats
next time we go to war

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.810
with zombie horse Franz Ferdinand.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.190
The Jones Act not only requires

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.740
that vessels undergoing
cabotage be American owned,

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.160
it also requires that
they be American made,

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.220
which means if you wanna fly
old stripey on your boat,

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:36.570
that freighter better be
built in the United States.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.730
American built coastal
and feeder ships cost

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.030
between 190 million and
250 million dollars,

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.490
whereas the cost of a similar vessel

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.950
of the foreign shipyard
is only 30 million.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.300
So the American companies,

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.120
which the Jones Act theoretically wants

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.560
to call upon next time
we go to a horse war,

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.350
can only buy one American ship

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.240
instead of eight foreign ships.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.140
Just a friendly reminder,
ships are inanimate objects

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.450
and it doesn't matter where they're built.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.710
They don't have accents
or passports or souls.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.650
All things being equally floaty,

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.000
buy the ship that's cheapest

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.980
and hoist a flag of your choice.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.800
In the United States where
we restrict cabotage,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.830
only two percent of our
freight travels by sea,

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.620
whereas in the European Union

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.930
where member states can
freely engage in cabotage

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.730
between them, or as they
call it, cabotage a trois,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.030
40% of freighting is done by ship.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.510
Instead, because we've
made shipping more costly

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:29.210
we rely on trucks which are more expensive

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.210
and carbon-intensive than ships.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.600
Also, I don't know about you,

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.710
I have never been stuck behind
a steamship on I-95 before.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.030
The Jones Act exists to try to
expand our shipping capacity

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.800
and make us self-reliant,
unlike the Norah Jones Act,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.690
which is the soundtrack
I cry to in the bathtub.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:50.160
Anyway, we're a net exporter
of natural gas and yet in 2019,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.460
because there weren't enough
pipes to transport natural gas

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.300
from Southern States to Massachusetts,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.760
nor enough Jones Act
compliant vessels to do so,

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.160
Massachusetts had to
import it from Russia.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.080
Whenever we have a crisis,

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.240
the United States government
temporarily rescends

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.380
the Jones Act so that shippers can cheaply

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.860
and quickly get food and
materials and blob them

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.190
into the affected area.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:13.180
Then when the crisis
recedes, we reinstate it.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.060
The reason that stopping
the Jones Act works

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.750
during these times is
because, follow me here,

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.230
the Jones Act doesn't work.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.340
So why not permanently scrap it?

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.170
Well that's, because of lobbyists.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.070
That's why, (beep) lobbyists.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.360
According to a 2019 study by the OACD,

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.070
the US economic gains would be somewhere

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.940
between 19 billion and 64 billion dollars.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.640
Now I realized that 64
billion dollars isn't

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.650
even worth the Senator
getting out of bed for anymore

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.610
but somebody has to keep an
eye on the pocket change.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.100
Given that the Jones Act
counter-productively shrinks

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.470
our shipping capacity and
Merchant Mariner Fleet,

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.590
makes life more expensive
for Islanders and is directly

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.720
and obviously harmful every
single time we have a hurricane

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.470
or Godzilla attack, in
that time we scrap it.

